EXT. ABANDONED DRIVE-IN THEATRE - NIGHT

A cracked lot of weeds and speaker posts. A huge screen, blank and peeling, glows faintly under the moon.

On the hood of a rust-pitted pickup, two teenagers share a thermos.

CORNELIUS "NEELY" JAMES-OKONKWO, 17, in a letterman jacket two sizes too big, pours coffee into the cap. He is trying very hard to look relaxed.

Beside him, LUCINDA "LUCY" ARAUJO-PRICE, 17, in a flannel and combat boots, swings her legs and counts stars.

NEELY
Dad used to bring me here.

LUCY
Before they closed it?

NEELY
Before everything.

LUCY
What did you watch?

NEELY
Whatever was on. Monster movies, mostly.

LUCY
Scary?

NEELY
Not to him.

She laughs. Takes the cap. Sips. Makes a face.

LUCY
This is terrible.

NEELY
It's my grandmother's recipe.

LUCY
Your grandmother hated you.

NEELY
Possibly.

They sit. Crickets. The screen creaks in the wind.

LUCY
I leave Friday.

NEELY
I know.

LUCY
You're not going to say anything?

NEELY
I'm saying it. I'm saying "I know."

LUCY
That's not saying.

NEELY
It's most of what I've got.

She hands back the cap. Their fingers touch. Neither pulls away.

LUCY
There's a car.

NEELY
Where?

LUCY
Behind the screen. Headlights.

He looks. Two white eyes crawl along the fence line.

NEELY
Probably nothing.

LUCY
It's stopping.

The headlights go dark. A door opens. A figure walks toward them across the lot, hands in pockets.

BARNABY "OLD BARN" HOLLINGSWORTH, 60s, in a security jacket, flashlight swinging, whistling a tuneless song.

OLD BARN
Evening, kids.

NEELY
Evening, Mr. Hollingsworth.

OLD BARN
Thought I'd find you here.

NEELY
You knew?

OLD BARN
Your father told me. Before he passed.

Neely goes quiet. Lucy touches his sleeve.

OLD BARN (CONT'D)
He said, "If the boy ever comes out here with somebody, tell him there's a reel in the projection booth. Third shelf. Marked 'Neely.'"

NEELY
A reel.

OLD BARN
He never said what's on it.

NEELY
(slowly)
Is the projector--

OLD BARN
Still works. I oiled her last week. Don't ask me why.

Lucy slides off the hood. Takes Neely's hand.

LUCY
Come on.

They cross the lot, Old Barn lighting the way. The flashlight beam swings across the blank screen and, far above, the first flicker of an old image begins to shimmer.
